WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.040
Looking for a job as a makeup artist, teaching
ballroom dancing or blow drying hair?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.799
In some parts of the country you'll need government
certification

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.380
before anyone can pay you for these services
or face jail time.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.600
Occupational licensing laws, which apply to
one in three US jobs,

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.619
restrict consumer choice by protecting businesses
from competition.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.900
They also impose substantial costs on job
seekers.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.840
Arizona has one of the nation's most heavily
regulated labor markets

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.960
but now the state's businessman turned governor
Doug Ducey,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.550
who's the former CEO of Cold Stone Creamery,

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.760
has made occupational licensing reform a priority.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.900
What I wanted Arizona to be is the best place
in the country to live, work and do business

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.000
and part of that is beginning a business as
well as scaling a business

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.640
and that was our focus on improving that structure
of government

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.520
and really stopping the bullies that were
part of the boards and commissions.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.219
Since occupational licensing laws are particular
to each state,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.200
if you're a certified hair dryer say in Virginia,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.560
that doesn't mean you can move to Arizona
and just start working.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.680
First you have to complete a thousand hours
of training

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.900
before you can obtain a state cosmetology
license.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.080
Governor Ducey is backing a new law that would
change that.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.800
Just because someone packs up that moving
van in Chicago Illinois

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.800
they don't lose their skills on the way to
the state of Arizona.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.260
So why should somebody have to suffer the
burden of thousands of dollars

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:31.600
or weeks or months of re-certification in
a skill that they already have?

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.540
We had a tough time figuring out how many
regulations there are in the state of Arizona

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:40.690
with a cracker jack staff it took us probably
18 months

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:44.460
to figure out there were 11,000 regulations
in the state.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.480
In 2017, Ducey issued an executive order requiring
that state licensing boards

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.100
review and provide justification for rules
the Governor's office deemed excessive.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.860
The next day he signed the Right to Earn A
Living Act

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.640
which restricted state boards from issuing
any new occupational licensing rules

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.800
that couldn't be justified on health and safety
grounds.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.060
I think it's important that we remember who
the voters are and who the citizens are

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.920
and we're here to serve them.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:15.320
Too many of these boards and commissions exist
to stop competition

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:20.520
to stifle and protect the status quo and we're
changing that in Arizona.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:25.600
My issue is that we don't really know what
the standards are in these other states

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.280
and so why should we dumb down our standards
just to deregulate basically?

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.360
I mean I see this as sort of deregulation
for the sake of deregulation.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.900
Representative Pamela Powers Hannley of Tuscon
is opposed to the legislation.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.480
What I see here is, you know, over and over
and over again, you know,

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.610
throwing out licenses and certifications

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:49.980
and there was other bills that were proposed
in the House this year

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.540
that would go even farther than this as far
as deregulating occupations.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.260
and I think at some point it gets a little
risky for the populace.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:03.720
How so? I mean, 'cause if you, if you're successful
in another state doing this

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:08.520
I mean it's not like those skills don't, stop
when you come into this state.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.840
Well yes but with this we're only asking for
one year of experience

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.270
I mean what's the definition of successful?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.520
And then also how are we checking up on these
people?

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.480
What about this idea of public safety?

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:23.520
because I do think there's a fear that you're
actually going to attract people

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.220
from states that have lower standards than Arizona.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:32.260
Public health and public safety is always
going to be a priority for this administration

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:35.060
we're going to work with the individuals that
are coming

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.300
and with the licensing boards in which they came from

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.840
to make sure they're making good decisions.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:47.360
But I'm confident with the legislation we
have, with the guardrails and details it involves

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.740
that we'll be bringing qualified people here

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.160
and ultimately it will be the opportunities
that determine their success.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.160
Arizona's over regulated labor market drew
public attention in 2017.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.080
When it came out that a student barber named
Juan Carlos Montes De Oca

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.680
was being investigated by the state cosmetology
board

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.240
for giving haircuts to homeless vets without
a license.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:17.800
The bullies at the state cosmetology board
sought to stop him and stall his career

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.500
because he hadn't yet kissed their ring.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.480
We just thought that he was just doing a good
act for people that were in need.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.180
And this was a young person just in the formative
years of their career.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.040
We thought that was the wrong thing to do

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.630
and we were very pleasantly surprised by the
response that we received from the electorate

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:41.780
saying 'yes we don't need this overreach,
we don't need this overregulation.'

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.840
The new bill recognizing out of state certification
recently passed the House

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.560
and is currently under consideration in the
state Senate.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.180
We still have to prove it in the marketplace,

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.880
we still need to get it through both houses of the legislature.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.220
Ducey credits his deregulatory agenda for
Arizona's booming economy.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.840
We're the fourth fastest growing state in
the nation.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.680
Maricopa county where we are here in greater
Pheonix

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.180
is the number one fastest growing county in
America two years running.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:14.610
We're a state that has 70% of the adults here
were born somewhere other than the state of Arizona.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:18.300
I don't think that there's a better leading
indicator in this country

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.440
than that people pack up a U Haul truck and
say 'that's where I want to move to.'

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.580
In the game of states people vote with their
feet and Arizona's winning.

